# Build-context excludes (context = pipewire_audio_router/). The frontend stage
# runs its own `npm ci` and the Rust stage its own `cargo build`, so no build
# output from the host belongs in the context at all.
#
# Patterns are UNANCHORED (**/) on purpose: a bare `bridge-daemon/target`
# matches only that one path and silently let the nested vendored build caches
# through — bridge-daemon/vendor/{sendspin,airplay2-sender,shairplay}/target
# are ~8.6G of host-arch Rust artifacts that cargo inside the container never
# reads (path deps build into the root /build/target). That made the context
# ~8.8G, uploaded to the buildx builder on every single deploy.
**/target
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.git

# Not referenced by any COPY: docs/ is developer documentation, and
# bridge-daemon/dist/ is a locally built binary from scripts/build-daemon.sh.
docs
